WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.380
A brain region long-described only as a listening area also plans each spoken word a quarter

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:12.360
second ahead. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 250. How that patch of cortex assembles

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:18.760
a word, a blood marker for chronic traumatic encephalopathy, and muscle kept during obesity treatment.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.300
Wernicke's area in finding science news draws from a paper published today in science occupies

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.420
a temporal lobe patch above the left ear. Direct neural recordings captured activity

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:34.840
there while people attempted to speak. The measurements were taken during speech attempts,

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.500
not during passive listening. Researchers note the map could guide future brain implant designs

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:46.815
for restoring speech after injury. Something most people get wrong is treating that patch as a purely

00:00:46.815 --> 00:00:53.055
receptive zone that only decodes incoming language. The cortex there is assembling the motor commands

00:00:53.055 --> 00:00:58.335
for speech. The activity is not a reaction to sound already in the air. It is the brain

00:00:58.335 --> 00:01:03.755
putting those commands in order while the next word is still being formed. That sequence matches a

00:01:03.755 --> 00:01:09.635
familiar bodily fact. You often know the shape of a sentence before your mouth moves. Future speech

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:15.315
restoration implants may read those planning signals from this location rather than waiting for downstream

00:01:15.315 --> 00:01:23.656
motor areas. Elevated EMTBR TOW-243 in blood samples The New York Times Reports showed up in

00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:29.656
people later confirmed to have chronic traumatic encephalopathy at autopsy. Independent replication

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:35.356
supported the initial observation. The finding offers the first potential anti-mortem test for the

00:01:35.356 --> 00:01:41.247
condition. Middle-aged and older adults who lifted weights in a clinical trial nature-published,

00:01:41.247 --> 00:01:45.467
Retained more muscle mass and strength while taking obesity medications.

00:01:45.627 --> 00:01:50.687
The trial measured changes in lean mass and physical function across the intervention period.

00:01:51.575 --> 00:01:57.755
A UC Berkeley molecule, according to Science Daily, increased energy burn by up to 18% in

00:01:57.755 --> 00:01:58.015
mice.

00:01:58.595 --> 00:02:01.735
The treatment lowered liver fat and improved glucose control.

00:02:02.275 --> 00:02:04.775
Animals lost weight while muscle was preserved.

00:02:05.255 --> 00:02:10.315
Combining the compound with GLP1 drugs produced larger effects than either treatment alone.

00:02:10.315 --> 00:02:16.300
current AI systems in workfizz.org highlights can predict disease risk from

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.820
genetic variants but cannot yet explain why disease occurs or which drug will

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.160
work. New virtual cell frameworks are being built to simulate how specific

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.740
mutations and compounds alter cellular behavior. The goal is to move from

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:35.429
correlation to mechanistic forecasts inside individual cells. Embarry's research

00:02:35.429 --> 00:02:39.709
vessel Paragon deployed three autonomous robots in Monterey Bay in early

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:45.609
October. The platforms will collect simultaneous physical, chemical, and biological measurements

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:50.929
over extended periods. The effort is meant to create a persistent, high-resolution picture

00:02:50.929 --> 00:02:57.721
of changing ocean conditions. MIT modeling shows that power demand for AI data centers increases

00:02:57.721 --> 00:03:03.841
fine particle and ozone formation in downwind regions. The pollution travels hundreds of kilometers

00:03:03.841 --> 00:03:09.221
from the facilities themselves. Health impacts therefore appear in communities that host none of

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:14.919
the servers. University of Sydney researchers compared galaxy simulations spanning billions

00:03:14.919 --> 00:03:19.779
of years with mass or observations. They found the Milky Way's central bar creates

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:24.999
shock fronts that compress gas and trigger star birth along its leading edge. The bar

00:03:24.999 --> 00:03:31.199
extends roughly 4.3 kiloparsecs and rotates slowly. Part of the structure previously labeled

00:03:31.199 --> 00:03:36.799
the Norma spiral arm aligns instead with this bar driven shock front. Lead author Hillary

00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:41.119
Secretary Davis noted the bar's properties have been highly debated because dust obscures

00:03:41.119 --> 00:03:41.999
direct views.

00:03:42.939 --> 00:03:48.479
Harvard engineers stack two layers of titanium dioxide nanostructures, so the upper pillars

00:03:48.479 --> 00:03:50.279
match the geometry below them.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:55.819
The design supplies point-by-point anti-reflection across the entire surface without a separate

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:56.179
coating.

00:03:56.739 --> 00:04:01.699
The approach also opens extra degrees of freedom for polarization control and acromatic

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:02.299
performance.

00:04:02.299 --> 00:04:07.399
The work appears in nature nanotechnology and builds on a collaboration with corning

00:04:07.399 --> 00:04:08.159
incorporated.

00:04:09.031 --> 00:04:14.011
University of Nottingham scientists tested the commercial barley variety, S.Y. Kestrel,

00:04:14.551 --> 00:04:17.811
carrying the RIDE 4-HB locus from a wild relative.

00:04:18.431 --> 00:04:23.911
Airborne chemicals reduced aphids settling by more than 75% compared with a related line.

00:04:24.591 --> 00:04:28.011
Aphids that did land struggled to feed continuously from the flome.

00:04:28.011 --> 00:04:33.791
The plants also restricted barley-yellow dwarf virus replication and maintained photosynthetic

00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:34.951
output under attack.

00:04:35.551 --> 00:04:40.916
The study is published in New Phytologist, a tiny ran that disappeared from an island

00:04:40.916 --> 00:04:47.216
off Stewart Island around 1972, was the final bird species lost in Aotero, New Zealand.

00:04:47.796 --> 00:04:52.936
Its extinction pattern highlights how small, isolated populations remain vulnerable even

00:04:52.936 --> 00:04:54.676
after broader threats are reduced.

00:04:54.676 --> 00:05:00.779
Researchers are assembling multiple discrete optical components into compact three-dimensional

00:05:00.779 --> 00:05:05.539
arrangements that shape amplitude, phase, and polarization simultaneously.

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:11.239
The approach reduces the alignment challenges of traditional flat-optic setups while expanding

00:05:11.239 --> 00:05:14.699
possible beam properties for imaging and quantum applications.

